      "sourceHash": "78abed82d125a6f940fc9441be05b110713409ef585a50b7d02901beec07dc7d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.98,
          "end": 6.15,
          "en": "Dynamic components are a very useful feature which can save you some code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.22,
          "end": 13.65,
          "en": "Another useful feature are recursive components, and the typical example here is if you want to render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 13.65,
          "end": 14.91,
          "en": "a tree structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 18.12,
          "en": "Now what do I mean with tree structure?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "Let's ignore our dynamic component code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "Let's say in the app Svelte file, we have some data that could of course also be coming from a store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 29.39,
          "en": "That's our.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 30.8,
          "end": 33.47,
          "en": "Family structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 34.59,
          "end": 38.4,
          "en": "Which could be an array where we have a couple of elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 38.55,
          "end": 42.66,
          "en": "Each element has a is parent property, which is true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.69,
          "end": 43.98,
          "en": "Then maybe a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 50.91,
          "en": "And I'm just coming up with some names here like Chris and here we have is parent True.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "Name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 54.19,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "Anna and then we might have nested data in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 58.3,
          "end": 65.95,
          "en": "So here we have some children where we again have a similar structure and each child could be a parent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.19,
          "end": 67.54,
          "en": "and has a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 68.77,
          "end": 73.09,
          "en": "Mo and then it can in turn have some children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.09,
          "end": 80.02,
          "en": "And then at some point we might be at an element which is not apparent, just has a name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 81.13,
          "end": 81.99,
          "en": "Julie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 82.57,
          "end": 87.52,
          "en": "Now here we have some slightly nested data and now let's say we want to reflect that in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 87.52,
          "end": 89.59,
          "en": "because we're painting some family tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 89.62,
          "end": 97.99000000000001,
          "en": "For example, for this I'll add a family node, dot svelte file, and in that family node, dot svelte",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 97.99000000000001,
          "end": 108.94,
          "en": "file, I have my script tags, of course, where I get my family or just my member prop like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 109.81,
          "end": 114.88,
          "en": "Here I have my H1 tag where I output my member name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 116.2,
          "end": 121.69,
          "en": "Then below that I have an unordered list where I want to display my children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 121.84,
          "end": 123.1,
          "en": "I'm not doing this right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 128.83,
          "en": "Now we can use that family node here in the apps world file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 128.83,
          "end": 130.06,
          "en": "Let's import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 130.09,
          "end": 136.54,
          "en": "Import family node from dot slash family node dot svelte like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 136.75,
          "end": 141.13,
          "en": "And now let's output the family structure with the help of the family node here, shall we?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 141.46,
          "end": 143.86,
          "en": "So here we can use a good old each loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 146.9,
          "end": 149,
          "en": "Family structure as.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 150.04,
          "end": 154.36,
          "en": "Family member each.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 155.93,
          "end": 160.22,
          "en": "Now I use my family node here and there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 160.22,
          "end": 163.82,
          "en": "I pass my member and that is family member like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 164.98,
          "end": 166.18,
          "en": "For now, save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 166.99,
          "end": 170.62,
          "en": "I got Chris and Anna here, which are my two top level elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 171.07,
          "end": 177.91,
          "en": "Now, of course, these elements themselves, and I should set this to false here by on Anna, these",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 177.91,
          "end": 180.88,
          "en": "elements themselves might have children, which are one output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 180.88,
          "end": 184.51,
          "en": "Chris, for example, has children, one child at least.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 185.2,
          "end": 188.32,
          "en": "The problem is this loop here, of course, is not nested.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 188.32,
          "end": 192.1,
          "en": "So I need a loop inside of family node, which is where I receive my member here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 192.1,
          "end": 193.72,
          "en": "I want to output my children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 193.9,
          "end": 197.35,
          "en": "So in here I can again add a loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 199.21,
          "end": 202.15,
          "en": "To loop through the children of that family member.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 202.27,
          "end": 208.48,
          "en": "So a loop through member children, at least if this member has children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 208.48,
          "end": 214.96,
          "en": "So first of all, I'll add a if check and see if member is parent and only if the member is a parent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 214.96,
          "end": 218.71,
          "en": "then I want to render this unordered list because otherwise there are no children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 219.07,
          "end": 221.8,
          "en": "So then I want to go through children here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 225.18,
          "en": "As a child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 226.54,
          "end": 227.89,
          "en": "Now, what do I want to output here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 228.65,
          "end": 230.03,
          "en": "Of course I could output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 231.07,
          "end": 237.16,
          "en": "List item in here where I simply output the child name because child again is a family member with a",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 237.16,
          "end": 237.64,
          "en": "name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 237.64,
          "end": 240.1,
          "en": "So if we save that, we see Mo here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 240.1,
          "end": 245.15,
          "en": "But please note that Mo also has a child.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 245.17,
          "end": 251.98,
          "en": "Mo is also a parent with a child, and that is where we reach a problem instead here I maybe want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 251.98,
          "end": 255.37,
          "en": "render this family node component again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 256.76,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "The semantically not in an unordered list then, but simply below this member name here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "Let me add a horizontal line below all of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 268.76,
          "end": 269.69,
          "en": "How could we achieve that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 269.69,
          "end": 274.43,
          "en": "We would need to render family node from inside family node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 274.90999999999997,
          "end": 279.38,
          "en": "And that is exactly where svelte self helps you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 279.40999999999997,
          "end": 285.33,
          "en": "As the name suggests, this allows you to render the same component you're already in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 285.35,
          "end": 290.6,
          "en": "It's like a recursive function call and here to svelte self.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 290.6,
          "end": 296.96,
          "en": "I can therefore pass the member prop again because we need that member prop and that would be child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 296.96,
          "end": 297.5,
          "en": "here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 297.53,
          "end": 299.15,
          "en": "Now if we save that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 299.9,
          "end": 302.63,
          "en": "We see Chris with Mo and Julie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 302.66,
          "end": 305.34,
          "en": "Now, regarding the styling I chose here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 305.36,
          "end": 312.46,
          "en": "It's not really clear how these are all related, but of course we know our data here is reflected correctly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 312.47,
          "end": 316.12,
          "en": "Chris has a child named Mo and Mo has a child named Julie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 316.13,
          "end": 319.4,
          "en": "That is why we see Chris and then Mo and then Julie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 319.4,
          "end": 322.33,
          "en": "And then the three horizontal lines here and then Anna.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 322.34,
          "end": 327.14,
          "en": "So of course you could work on the styling to indent this all and make this a bit clearer, a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 327.14,
          "end": 327.8,
          "en": "to grasp.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 327.8,
          "end": 330.83,
          "en": "But I think this is also clear like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 330.83,
          "end": 334.52,
          "en": "Well, if you wanted to, of course you could wrap that all in a div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 337.3,
          "end": 337.96,
          "en": "That.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 339.07,
          "end": 342.55,
          "en": "Move the horizontal line and then here, simply add some styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 343.29,
          "end": 349.40999999999997,
          "en": "Where you say that the div should have some margin left of two REM and if you do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 350.23,
          "end": 352.26,
          "en": "And you see the structure a bit better.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 352.27,
          "end": 359.2,
          "en": "So recursive components are really useful if you are rendering such a folder structure or whenever you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 359.2,
          "end": 364.63,
          "en": "have a dependency on yourself, not a scenario you encounter all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 364.63,
          "end": 368.17,
          "en": "But as you see, definitely also not totally unrealistic.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
